{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 1, :comments ["<b>If the thief be found breaking in.</b> At night, for by day he would not break in, and the verse that comes after it is a witness: \"if the sun has risen.\"" "<b>He has no blood.</b> There is no bloodshed liability upon the one who kills him. And one may wonder at the commentators who say \"living blood\" — if so, what is \"a man of blood\" (II Samuel 16:8), \"his blood is upon him\" (Leviticus 20:9)?"], :book :exodus, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 22, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Piotrkow, 1907-1911" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH990020973480205171/NLI"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:37:15.569247769Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}